    <Label Name="Title" Style="GalleryTitle" Text="Continuous Deformations" Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="36.25" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
    <Label Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="A formula moves every point D of the pink circle to a new place E. As D runs around the circle, E draws the blue curve.\n\nPoint F sits on the segment from D to E. Its path, the purple curve, is a shape in between the two.\n\nDrag F along its segment to morph the circle into the blue curve and back. The thin curves are the steps in between. Drag A to resize the circle, or C to move it." Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="84.25" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
